{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>And Yaakov gave to Esav</b> etc. — together with the money he gave him for the purchase, he gave him bread and lentil stew, as testimony to the validity of the sale, as is the way of all purchasers of a transaction. And so we find: 'and he called his brothers to eat bread' — in the covenant between Yaakov and Lavan." "<b>And Esav despised the birthright.</b> Before Aharon was chosen for the priesthood, the divine service was performed by the firstborn. That wicked man said: what — I should soil my hands with the sacrifices? As it is written: 'for blood you hated and blood pursued you' — the blood of circumcision and the blood of sacrifices. Another interpretation: because he did not want them to consider him a fool for having sold his birthright, he would disparage it and say it was worth only a trifle; but in the end he regretted it, as it is written: 'my birthright he took.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:06:00.734290773Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}